## Infrastructure Issues & Limitations

1. SPOF (Single Point of Failure)

The load balancer is a Single Point of Failure. If it goes down, users cannot access the web servers.

The Primary database is also a potential SPOF for write operations. If it fails, the application cannot perform writes until recovery or failover occurs.

2. Security Issues

There are no firewalls in this infrastructure to filter and control network traffic.

There is also no HTTPS or SSL/TLS encryption, meaning traffic between users and the infrastructure may be transmitted without encryption.

3. No Monitoring

There is no monitoring system to track server health, resource usage, errors, or application performance.

As a result, failures and performance problems may go unnoticed until users report them.
